.Dd June 25, 2026
.Dt VCAN 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vcan
.Nd virtual Controller Area Network interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options CAN"
.Pp
.Nm ifconfig Cm vcan Ns Ar N Cm create
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a virtual CAN network interface with no associated hardware.
It is the CAN analogue of the loopback interface: every frame transmitted on a
.Nm
interface is delivered to all
.Xr can 4
sockets bound to that interface.
It is useful for development and for testing CAN applications without a bus.
.Pp
A
.Nm
interface is created with
.Cm ifconfig vcan Ns Ar N Cm create
and removed with
.Cm ifconfig vcan Ns Ar N Cm destroy .
Its MTU is large enough to carry a CAN FD frame, so both classic and FD frames
are supported.
.Pp
A
.Nm
interface is not IP-capable and carries only CAN frames.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr can 4 ,
.Xr slcan 4 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
